CARLA ue58-dev: the terrain of a map generated from OpenDRIVE dips under water.

CARLA 1.0 fits a terrain surface to the road heights over the whole generated map (AOpenDriveGenerator::
GenerateGroundPlane). Over a river or a harbour it spreads at the banks' and dikes' height, so the water of
coupled-carla's scenery (flat tiles at the water body's level) lies under it and ships sail through grass (Hoek van
Holland, 2026-11-27: terrain at 1.3-5.9 m over the Nieuwe Waterweg, water at 1.1 m). The Python API cannot hide or
lower it (no parameter, no environment object).

coupled-carla now sends the scenery's water bodies with the OpenDRIVE as a <userData code="coupledcarla.water">
element (placement.carla_xodr: one closed ring a line, "<body> <level m> x,y x,y ...", CARLA metres). This patch reads
it and, at every terrain vertex inside a body (even-odd over its rings, so islands stay land) that is not under
pavement, lowers the terrain to 3 m below the body's level. Without the userData nothing changes.

Apply in a CARLA ue58-dev tree (checked against 70f9085): git apply <this file>; then rebuild the editor (lin5080:
~/build_editor58.sh) and, for the packaged server, the package (win5090 task cc58-package). Not posted upstream.

